title: Game Over.
new-page: true
go-to: eg_menu
on-arrival: {!
Q.game_over = 1;
Q.inflation_2 = Q.inflation.toFixed(1);
Q.unemployment_2 = Q.unemployment.toFixed(1);
Q.governed = (Q.term_start_time > 0) ? 1 : 0;
Q.reelected = (Q.governed && Q.n_elections >= Q.final_election && Q.result_type >= 1 && Q.result_type <= 4 && !Q.ousted) ? 1 : 0;
// won power at the last election, after losing in 1979
Q.late_victory = (!Q.governed && Q.result_type >= 1 && Q.result_type <= 4 && !Q.ousted) ? 1 : 0;
if (Q.late_victory) {
    this.achieve('second_chance');
}
this.achieve('game_completed');
if (Q.governed) {
    this.achieve('prime_minister');
}
if (Q.reelected) {
    this.achieve('re_elected');
    if (Q.result_type == 1 && Q.con_majority >= 100) {
        this.achieve('landslide');
    }
    if (Q.wet_dissent < 20 && Q.dry_dissent < 20) {
        this.achieve('one_nation');
    }
    if (Q.inflation < 5 && Q.union_power <= 40 && Q.privatisations >= 3 && Q.right_to_buy_progress >= 3) {
        this.achieve('thatcherism');
    }
    if (Q.u_turn == -1) {
        this.achieve('lady_for_turning');
    }
    if (Q.unemployment < 8) {
        this.achieve('full_employment');
    }
}
if (Q.governed && Q.u_turn == 1) {
    this.achieve('not_for_turning');
}
if (Q.falklands == 3) {
    this.achieve('rejoice');
}
if (Q.falklands == 6) {
    this.achieve('deterrence');
}
if (Q.eec_rebate >= 2) {
    this.achieve('money_back');
}
if (Q.ousted) {
    this.achieve('et_tu');
}
if (Q.result_type == 5 && !Q.governed) {
    this.achieve('sunny_jim');
}
if (Q.autumn_election_1978 && Q.governed) {
    this.achieve('waiting_at_the_church');
}
if (Q.reelected) {
    if (Q.nhs_funding >= 2 && !Q.cprs_defended) {
        this.achieve('nhs_safe');
    }
    if (Q.historical_mode) {
        this.achieve('tina');
    } else if (Q.difficulty >= 1) {
        this.achieve('iron_lady');
    }
    if (!Q.unemployment_3m && Q.unemployment < 11) {
        this.achieve('never_three_million');
    }
    if (Q.result_type == 1 && Q.con_majority >= 144) {
        this.achieve('big_majority');
    }
}
if (Q.governed && !Q.ousted && Q.inflation < 4) {
    this.achieve('sound_money');
}
if (Q.privatisations >= 5) {
    this.achieve('share_owning');
}
if (Q.governed && Q.union_power <= 30) {
    this.achieve('union_power_broken');
}
!}
face-image: img/events/thatcher_1980.jpg
on-display: {!
if (typeof window !== 'undefined' && window.playMoment) {
    var sad = Q.ousted || (Q.governed && Q.result_type == 5);
    window.playMoment(sad ? 'music/funeral_march.mp3' : 'music/god_save_the_queen.mp3');
}
!}

= The Verdict of History

@eg_menu

- #endings
- @end_game: End game.

#################### How it ended

@defeat_1979
title: Defeated, and defeated again.
view-if: result_type = 5 and governed = 0 and ousted = 0
tags: endings
go-to: eg_menu

[? if lab_mps >= majority_line : [+ lab_leader +] has won a majority of his own. ?][? if lab_mps < majority_line : [+ lab_leader +] carries on, at the head of the largest party in a hung parliament. ?] The post-war consensus has survived another election.

By the weekend, the Sunday papers are full of leadership speculation. Edward Heath lets it be known that he is available.

@late_victory_ending
title: Prime Minister at last.
view-if: late_victory = 1
tags: endings
go-to: eg_menu

After the long years in opposition, the country has turned to you. [? if result_type = 1 : With a majority of [+ con_majority +], ?][? if result_type >= 2 : Without a majority of your own, ?] you go to the Palace to kiss hands. The real work starts now.

@ousted_ending
title: Ousted by your own party.
view-if: ousted = 1
tags: endings
go-to: eg_menu

[? if governed = 1 : The men in grey suits came to Downing Street, and then the ballot of Conservative MPs did the rest. You leave Number 10 for the last time [+ months_in_office +] months after you arrived. ?][? if governed = 0 : Defeated at the polls and then by your own party, you return to the backbenches. ?] The new leader promises a return to One Nation conservatism and a gentler economic policy.

@defeat_reelection
title: Turned out of office.
view-if: result_type = 5 and governed = 1 and ousted = 0
tags: endings
go-to: eg_menu

[? if lab_mps >= majority_line : Labour, under [+ lab_leader +], has won a majority. ?][? if lab_mps < majority_line : Labour, under [+ lab_leader +], is the largest party in a hung parliament. ?] Your government lasted [+ months_in_office +] months. To your critics, the experiment has been tried and has failed. To your admirers, it was abandoned too soon.

@landslide_reelection
title: Re-elected by a landslide.
view-if: reelected = 1 and result_type = 1 and con_majority >= 100
tags: endings
go-to: eg_menu

A majority of [+ con_majority +]. The country has endorsed not just a government but a new settlement. The wets are finished as a force, and the next Parliament is yours to shape.

@comfortable_reelection
title: Re-elected.
view-if: reelected = 1 and result_type = 1 and con_majority < 100
tags: endings
go-to: eg_menu

A majority of [+ con_majority +]. Not a landslide, but a second term, something no Conservative government has managed since 1959.

@hung_reelection
title: Clinging on.
view-if: reelected = 1 and result_type >= 2
tags: endings
go-to: eg_menu

You remain in Downing Street, but without a majority of your own. [? if result_type = 2 : The Ulster Unionists hold the balance of power. ?][? if result_type = 3 : The price of power is electoral reform. ?][? if result_type = 4 : Every vote in the new Parliament will be a struggle. ?]

#################### The record in government

@inflation_beaten
title: Inflation has been beaten.
view-if: governed = 1 and inflation < 5
tags: endings
go-to: eg_menu

Inflation is down to [+ inflation_2 +]%, the lowest in more than a decade. Sound money was the promise, and it has been kept.

@inflation_high
title: Inflation still rages.
view-if: governed = 1 and inflation >= 10
tags: endings
go-to: eg_menu

Inflation is still [+ inflation_2 +]%. The central promise of the government has not been kept.

@mass_unemployment
title: Three million unemployed.
view-if: governed = 1 and unemployment >= 11
tags: endings
go-to: eg_menu

Unemployment stands at [+ unemployment_2 +]%. Whole towns in the North, Scotland and Wales have lost the industries that built them, and they won't forget who was in charge.

@jobs_kept
title: The dole queues kept short.
view-if: governed = 1 and unemployment < 8
tags: endings
go-to: eg_menu

Unemployment is [+ unemployment_2 +]%, far below what the critics of monetarism predicted.

@unions_tamed
title: The unions brought within the law.
view-if: governed = 1 and union_power <= 40
tags: endings
go-to: eg_menu

Secret ballots, limits on picketing and the end of blanket legal immunities have shifted the balance of power in industry. [? if coal_stocks >= 2 : The coal stocks at the power stations are high; if the miners strike, the lights will stay on. ?]

@unions_unbowed
title: The unions are as strong as ever.
view-if: governed = 1 and union_power >= 65
tags: endings
go-to: eg_menu

The trade union barons still hold the whip hand. Whoever governs next will have to come to terms with them, or fight them.

@popular_capitalism
title: Popular capitalism.
view-if: governed = 1 and privatisations >= 3
tags: endings
go-to: eg_menu

[+ privatisations +] state enterprises have been returned to the private sector, and the queues for share offers are growing. The frontiers of the state are being rolled back.

@property_owning
title: A property-owning democracy.
view-if: governed = 1 and right_to_buy_progress >= 3
tags: endings
go-to: eg_menu

Hundreds of thousands of council tenants have bought their homes. Many of them will never vote Labour again.

@falklands_won
title: Rejoice.
view-if: falklands = 3
tags: endings
go-to: eg_menu

The Union Jack flies again over Port Stanley. Britain has shown it will fight for its own, and you have become a war leader.

@falklands_lost
title: The South Atlantic disaster.
view-if: falklands = 4
tags: endings
go-to: eg_menu

The task force failed. The Falkland Islands are now the Malvinas, and Britain's standing in the world has fallen further than at any time since Suez.

@falklands_negotiated
title: A deal over the Falklands.
view-if: falklands = 5
tags: endings
go-to: eg_menu

The islands passed to Argentine administration under an international settlement. Peace was kept; the right of the party will never forgive it.

@falklands_deterred
title: No war in the South Atlantic.
view-if: falklands = 6
tags: endings
go-to: eg_menu

HMS Endurance stayed on station, and the Argentine junta never risked it. History will never know what it was spared.

@money_back
title: "Our own money back."
view-if: eec_rebate >= 2
tags: endings
go-to: eg_menu

After years of handbag-swinging at European summits, Britain has won a permanent rebate on its contributions to the Community budget.

@not_for_turning_ending
title: The lady was not for turning.
view-if: governed = 1 and u_turn = 1
tags: endings
go-to: eg_menu

Through the worst of the recession, with the wets in revolt and 364 economists against you, you held the course. Whether that was courage or stubbornness, it is now the defining fact of your premiership.

@u_turn_ending
title: The U-turn.
view-if: governed = 1 and u_turn = -1
tags: endings
go-to: eg_menu

Like Heath before you, you turned. The government reflated and the dries despaired. To the consensus, it was common sense; to the believers, it was betrayal.

@alliance_ending
title: The Alliance.
view-if: alliance_formed = 1
tags: endings
go-to: eg_menu

Labour split, and the Social Democrats and Liberals together have reshaped the opposition. [? if lib_mps >= 40 : With [+ lib_mps +] MPs, the Alliance has broken the two-party system. ?][? if lib_mps < 40 : First-past-the-post has cheated them of the breakthrough their votes deserved. ?]

@nhs_safe_ending
title: "The NHS is safe with us."
view-if: governed = 1 and nhs_funding >= 2 and cprs_defended = 0
tags: endings
go-to: eg_menu

The health service was funded above inflation [+ nhs_funding +] times, and Labour's warnings that the Conservatives would dismantle it rang hollow. [? if prescription_charges >= 2 : The prescription charge went up, but the service itself is intact. ?][? if nhs_contracting = 1 : The cleaners and caterers now work for private contractors; the doctors and nurses still work for the state. ?]

@nhs_strain_ending
title: The health service under strain.
view-if: governed = 1 and (cprs_defended = 1 or (private_health = 1 and nhs_funding = 0))
tags: endings
go-to: eg_menu

Waiting lists are growing, and the government's commitment to a free health service is openly doubted. [? if cprs_defended = 1 : Nobody has forgotten the Think Tank's paper, or that you defended it. ?] Labour will make the NHS the centre of every campaign for a generation.

@pensions_ending
title: Pensions tied to prices.
view-if: governed = 1 and pension_link_broken = 1
tags: endings
go-to: eg_menu

Breaking the link between pensions and earnings saved little at first. It will save a fortune by the end of the century, and the pensioners of the 1990s will be correspondingly poorer than their parents expected.

@education_ending
title: Choice in education.
view-if: governed = 1 and (assisted_places = 1 or parental_choice = 1 or school_vouchers = 2)
tags: endings
go-to: eg_menu

[? if parental_choice = 1 : Parents can now state a preference for their school and read its exam results. ?] [? if assisted_places = 1 : Thousands of children from modest homes hold assisted places at independent schools. ?] [? if school_vouchers = 2 : In Kent, the voucher experiment is being watched by every education authority in the country. ?]

@erm_ending
title: Sterling in the Exchange Rate Mechanism.
view-if: erm = 1
tags: endings
go-to: eg_menu

The pound is tied to the Deutschmark. The City likes the stability; the monetarists say that interest rates are now set in Frankfurt. Whether the peg holds through the next recession is a question for another Parliament.

@rates_ending
title: "The rates must go."
view-if: rates_pledge = 1
tags: endings
go-to: eg_menu

The promise to abolish the domestic rates stands, and nobody has yet found anything to replace them. The civil servants still favour a flat-rate charge on every adult. Some ministers have started to call it the community charge, which sounds better than a poll tax.

@glc_ending
title: The end of the GLC.
view-if: glc_abolition = 1
tags: endings
go-to: eg_menu

The Greater London Council and the metropolitan counties are being abolished. Ken Livingstone has become a national figure fighting it, and London will have no city-wide government of its own for years to come.

@docklands_ending
title: The Docklands.
view-if: docklands = 1
tags: endings
go-to: eg_menu

On the Isle of Dogs, where the West India Docks once employed thousands, the developers are moving in. A light railway is planned, and an American consortium talks of a vast office development at Canary Wharf.

@nuclear_ending
title: Sizewell.
view-if: nuclear_programme = 1
tags: endings
go-to: eg_menu

The public inquiry into the Sizewell B reactor is still sitting, and will sit for years. If the plan survives it, the miners will never again be able to turn off the country's lights.

@to_be_continued
title: What comes next.
view-if: reelected = 1
tags: endings
go-to: eg_menu

This version of the game ends at your re-election. The second term, with the miners, Brighton, Westland and the Big Bang, is not written yet.

#################### Achievements

@achievements
title: Achievements
view-if: achievement_game_completed == 1
tags: endings
go-to: eg_menu if started == 1; root.start_menu_2 if started == 0

There are 57 achievements.

= In this playthrough

